WEBVTT

00:00:04.190 --> 00:00:07.560
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you.

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:10.890
Please hug me as tight as you can right now!

00:00:10.890 --> 00:00:14.100
Hold on tight to the warmth

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:20.630
that's sprouted inside my little heart.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:30.880
Never say "It's hopeless" and get down in the dumps!

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.310
Go! Go!

00:00:32.310 --> 00:00:37.690
Hold on till blue skies spread inside your heart.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.590
Always in the rainy days in my life!

00:00:41.100 --> 00:00:43.960
Always in the good days in my life!

00:00:44.430 --> 00:00:50.960
Never hesitate! Give all you've got! Never give up!

00:00:51.970 --> 00:00:55.340
Shaking my hands 'cuz I'm here for you!

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.780
Jumping as high as I can 'cuz I long for you!

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:01.910
The scenery reflected in your eyes

00:01:01.910 --> 00:01:05.390
is a memory I carry with me.

00:01:05.390 --> 00:01:08.750
Feeling my kick though I've sworn to help you,

00:01:08.750 --> 00:01:12.120
I make mistakes when maybe I shouldn't.

00:01:12.120 --> 00:01:15.520
It may hurt me deep inside my heart,

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:21.430
but with experience the clouds in there will clear away.

00:01:48.420 --> 00:01:51.420
Kazuya, shall I get you some milk?

00:01:52.190 --> 00:01:54.920
Um... Not now, thanks.

00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:57.680
I see...

00:02:08.510 --> 00:02:11.480
Oh! What an adorable landlady!

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:14.230
I'm not a landlady. I'm Rena.

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:18.070
I-I'm Kisaragi. Kisaragi, apartment 201.

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:21.790
I'm Rena, Kasumi's helper. Pleased to meet you!

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.360
Oh, how wonderful!

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:27.000
Maybe I should give you next month's rent, too!

00:02:27.970 --> 00:02:30.760
That's not the song you sing when <i>I</i> come for the money.

00:02:32.040 --> 00:02:34.720
Have your rent ready when we come back next month!

00:02:37.520 --> 00:02:40.820
Well, aside from Shikishima, we've got everybody's rent.

00:02:40.820 --> 00:02:41.760
Rena, darling...

00:02:42.330 --> 00:02:43.370
Rena?

00:02:43.370 --> 00:02:45.010
I feel very creepy for some reason.

00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:55.020
That should do it.

00:03:22.840 --> 00:03:25.680
Morning! Have you had breakfast yet?

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:27.820
Whoops...

00:03:29.220 --> 00:03:30.800
Kazuya, did you know?

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:34.400
Mr. Mitarai, who lives in apartment 103, is an amazing person.

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:37.700
He used to do research into aircraft that could link up and separate.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:39.690
M-My closet!

00:03:40.480 --> 00:03:45.430
It's a secret elevator, for you and me.

00:03:58.050 --> 00:04:02.360
What an odd reaction. You intrigue me more and more.

00:04:03.670 --> 00:04:07.230
I haven't eaten breakfast yet. May I have some?

00:04:07.230 --> 00:04:09.520
No, you can't! This is for Kazuya!

00:04:09.520 --> 00:04:11.770
Meaning I can make some for myself.

00:04:11.770 --> 00:04:16.460
Kei, what did you do to my closet? If the landlady ever finds out!

00:04:16.460 --> 00:04:17.730
Here!

00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:19.980
Could you both go out shopping for me?

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:21.040
Go on, hurry!

00:04:21.040 --> 00:04:21.900
Uh, but!

00:04:22.620 --> 00:04:25.100
Kazuya! Mr. Kisaragi said he <i>really</i> likes me!

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:25.890
No kidding.

00:04:25.890 --> 00:04:28.440
Kazuya, let's go out and play!

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:30.640
Uh... H-Hold on here!

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:36.420
I wanna play now! I wanna play now!

00:04:36.420 --> 00:04:40.790
Rena, you shouldn't put Kazuya on the spot like this.

00:04:41.900 --> 00:04:43.640
"How to boil an egg."

00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:48.790
"Fill a pot with some water. Add a pinch of salt. Bring water to boil, then add eggs..."

00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:52.290
How many CCs is "some water"? How many grams is a "pinch"?

00:04:52.690 --> 00:04:56.310
It's like we have a weirdo magnet around here.

00:04:56.310 --> 00:05:00.820
I'm not asking for anything special, just to go out and play, that's all.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:05.280
It's not raining. Kazuya should spend more time with me!

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:06.840
Huh? Kasumi? Hey!

00:05:06.840 --> 00:05:08.720
Shut up and come with me!

00:05:10.800 --> 00:05:13.300
Kazuya, about May...

00:05:13.300 --> 00:05:15.290
Do you absolutely <i>have</i> to give her back?

00:05:16.150 --> 00:05:16.750
Yeah...

00:05:16.750 --> 00:05:18.080
Isn't it weird?!

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:21.590
They suddenly send her to you and then just arbitrarily take her back?

00:05:21.590 --> 00:05:25.170
Even saying that, there's nothing I can do.

00:05:25.640 --> 00:05:29.510
That paper said I placed the order, and I can't pay for her.

00:05:29.510 --> 00:05:33.230
And you don't mind? They're taking May away!

00:05:33.230 --> 00:05:36.360
Look, I don't like it, but...

00:05:36.360 --> 00:05:37.480
But what?!

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:39.220
Here.

00:05:40.930 --> 00:05:42.940
Go out and enjoy the time you have left together.

00:05:42.940 --> 00:05:44.400
The weather's nice today.

00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.870
Right now?

00:05:45.870 --> 00:05:46.810
What's wrong?

00:05:47.320 --> 00:05:51.490
I wanted to clarify my data before May goes back, so...

00:05:53.450 --> 00:05:56.020
You don't have to do that <i>today</i>, do you?!

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:58.600
You're losing her soon, so do something nice for May!

00:05:58.600 --> 00:06:01.040
She's done so much for you already!

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.700
Kasumi! Shikishima's in!

00:06:07.700 --> 00:06:09.390
You can get the rent today!

00:06:09.390 --> 00:06:11.330
Gotcha! I'm on my way!

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:12.830
Kazuya...

00:06:12.830 --> 00:06:13.640
Yeah.

00:06:14.740 --> 00:06:16.390
Okay, let's go!

00:06:16.390 --> 00:06:18.350
Kasumi! Hurry! Hurry!

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:21.440
Kasumi, thank you for everything.

00:06:21.440 --> 00:06:22.810
May...

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.370
Come <i>on!</i> Let's go, Kasumi!

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:26.850
Have fun.

00:06:28.810 --> 00:06:30.210
Have fun?

00:06:30.740 --> 00:06:33.260
Looks like Shikishima's in trouble.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:34.600
Kazuya...

00:06:34.600 --> 00:06:37.250
Thank you for everything.

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:40.900
I know I'm small, and I haven't been much use, but—

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.680
Nice day, isn't it, May?

00:06:45.270 --> 00:06:49.260
Wanna go out for a while? We still have some time.

00:06:52.950 --> 00:06:53.890
Sure!

00:06:59.890 --> 00:07:02.350
WHAT?! You're leaving?!

00:07:02.350 --> 00:07:05.090
Why?! Why?! WHY?!

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:08.670
I wanted to see a look of horror on my hated enemy's face!

00:07:08.670 --> 00:07:13.950
Yes. As long as I recover Cyber Doll May, it's okay with me.

00:07:13.950 --> 00:07:19.290
I thought we gave him extra time to make Saotome suffer!

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.540
Are we just going to wait here quietly like this, Sara?!

00:07:21.540 --> 00:07:22.340
Yes.

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:24.750
Well, I'll be off, then.

00:07:25.450 --> 00:07:27.290
<i>My time here's running out, too.</i>

00:07:27.290 --> 00:07:29.560
<i>If I don't hurry, I won't get to eat any more ramen!</i>

00:07:30.210 --> 00:07:32.290
She's surprisingly indifferent.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:36.860
Hold it.

00:07:36.860 --> 00:07:41.490
While I'm doing this, Saotome's making some lovely "last memories" with the mini-bot!

00:07:41.490 --> 00:07:44.360
Looking and acting the way I don't think he should look or act!

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.940
I have to stop it!

00:07:47.170 --> 00:07:48.110
<i>Mika!</i>

00:07:49.110 --> 00:07:50.690
<i>Yamazaki!</i>

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:52.770
<i>MIKA!</i>

00:07:53.660 --> 00:07:54.970
<i>SAOTOME!</i>

00:07:54.970 --> 00:07:58.040
Saotome! Saotome! Where?! Where are you hiding?!

00:07:58.510 --> 00:07:59.400
Kazuya isn't here.

00:07:59.400 --> 00:08:00.630
WHAT?!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.210
You won't escape me!

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:06.970
<i>Yamazaki can only watch as Mika is taken away by the police.</i>

00:08:06.970 --> 00:08:09.130
<i>Will the winds of fate ever stop blowing them apart?!</i>

00:08:11.730 --> 00:08:13.800
We are... the Warriors of Justice!

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:15.280
LIVE REVIEW!

00:08:18.280 --> 00:08:19.760
Go! Go!

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:45.090
Hey! Kazuya, you just laughed at me!

00:09:03.140 --> 00:09:05.230
Cool...

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:25.040
Wanna go on it?

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:25.880
Sure!

00:09:31.090 --> 00:09:32.800
Where's Saotome?!

00:09:32.800 --> 00:09:34.520
Saotome! Where are you?!

00:09:35.360 --> 00:09:37.140
S-Saotome! Wha...?!

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:38.430
Get out!

00:09:38.430 --> 00:09:39.180
Saotome!

00:09:39.180 --> 00:09:40.690
Would you stay out?!

00:09:41.120 --> 00:09:42.620
WHERE'S SAOTOME?!

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:54.940
What's wrong, May?

00:09:54.940 --> 00:09:58.840
Kazuya, I really want to thank you for today.

00:09:58.840 --> 00:10:00.410
It was a lot of fun.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:02.540
For me, too.

00:10:02.540 --> 00:10:07.220
I... I'm little and wasn't really very useful...

00:10:07.220 --> 00:10:09.080
but until today, I've really...

00:10:09.080 --> 00:10:13.150
That's not true. For me...

00:10:13.150 --> 00:10:18.590
Thanks to you, the thing I wanted to make, that I thought was just a dream, became a possibility.

00:10:19.230 --> 00:10:21.100
Thank you, May.

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:32.520
I wish this Ferris wheel would stop right here.

00:10:35.280 --> 00:10:41.030
I won't be able to see Saotome's horrified face in this mess!

00:10:42.830 --> 00:10:47.990
For failure to render payment, I am reclaiming Cyber Doll May.

00:10:50.520 --> 00:10:51.810
Kazuya...

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.860
I'll never forget you, Kazuya.

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:07.410
Well, then...

00:11:19.690 --> 00:11:22.340
Until today, I've really...!

00:11:24.900 --> 00:11:25.990
May...

00:11:25.990 --> 00:11:28.980
Merchandise recovery is confirmed.

00:11:46.130 --> 00:11:47.070
May...

00:12:10.150 --> 00:12:10.870
<i>May...</i>

00:12:12.870 --> 00:12:14.450
<i>Dear Kazuya.</i>

00:12:14.450 --> 00:12:18.520
<i>I wasn't with you very long, but I had a lot of fun.</i>

00:12:18.520 --> 00:12:21.850
<i>I may have been little and not very good at taking care of you</i>

00:12:21.850 --> 00:12:26.370
<i>but you were so kind to me, and that made me so happy.</i>

00:12:26.370 --> 00:12:30.420
<i>I'm so glad I was able to meet you.</i>

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:34.190
<i>I wish I could see you again someday. Thank you.</i>

00:12:34.190 --> 00:12:37.190
<i>To Kazuya. From May.</i>

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:48.160
<i>All of you out there, turn off your electrical appliances when you're not using them.</i>

00:12:48.160 --> 00:12:51.050
<i>Turning from power to powerful heat, let's head over to our weather corner.</i>

00:12:51.050 --> 00:12:52.190
May?

00:12:52.190 --> 00:12:55.250
<i>Take it away, Kiyohara!</i>

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.060
<i>Hi, Kiyohara here.</i>

00:12:57.060 --> 00:13:01.530
<i>We'll be seeing really hot weather all across the country today.</i>

00:13:01.530 --> 00:13:04.010
Huh? Where is it?

00:13:06.220 --> 00:13:10.240
<i>Much hotter than yesterday's temperatures.</i>

00:13:10.240 --> 00:13:11.970
<i>So, if you go out, be sure to wear—</i>

00:13:14.230 --> 00:13:15.480
<i>a hat to cover up.</i>

00:13:17.020 --> 00:13:19.230
<i>Let's start with western Japan.</i>

00:13:21.030 --> 00:13:22.990
<i>Sunny in Kyushu and Okinawa-</i>

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:27.970
For example!

00:13:28.730 --> 00:13:29.910
For example?

00:13:42.520 --> 00:13:44.010
Good morning, May.

00:13:45.280 --> 00:13:47.650
Oh, good morning, Kazuya!

00:13:47.650 --> 00:13:49.140
It's going to be another nice day today!

00:13:49.140 --> 00:13:50.050
Sure is.

00:13:50.050 --> 00:13:50.870
Yeah!

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:26.880
Let's do our best today!

00:14:31.980 --> 00:14:33.120
Ikariya?

00:14:35.760 --> 00:14:39.330
The thing I want to make...

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:47.000
Prof. Yumi? It's Kazuya Saotome. Can you do me a favor, please?

00:15:40.020 --> 00:15:44.250
We cyber dolls function using the MAID system.

00:15:45.550 --> 00:15:47.080
<i>The MAID system, huh?</i>

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:51.260
<i>If I can make that, I can build May myself!</i>

00:16:00.300 --> 00:16:02.020
Welcome home!

00:16:02.020 --> 00:16:06.360
Oh, don't be afraid. I'm from the Cyberdyne Corporation.

00:16:07.290 --> 00:16:11.360
The Cyberdyne Corporation? Oh, where May's from?

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:13.070
Yes.

00:16:13.480 --> 00:16:17.910
Um, look. I'm really sorry for causing you any trouble.

00:16:18.400 --> 00:16:20.260
Oh, don't worry about it.

00:16:20.260 --> 00:16:22.970
You don't have to stand there talking. Please, come in and sit.

00:16:22.970 --> 00:16:24.480
It's quite messy, though.

00:16:24.480 --> 00:16:26.960
Uh, right...

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:42.540
Ah, there's nothing as good as milk, is there?!

00:16:42.540 --> 00:16:45.520
Um, excuse me, but what's your name?

00:16:48.720 --> 00:16:51.530
Sao... Uh, I mean... Um...

00:16:51.530 --> 00:16:53.200
Let's see...

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:56.910
Sa-Sa-Sa-Sa... Cyber-X is my name!

00:16:57.360 --> 00:17:00.120
Cyber... X, huh?

00:17:01.710 --> 00:17:05.710
I believe your cyber doll was repossessed undamaged yesterday.

00:17:05.710 --> 00:17:10.170
I was using her without paying for it. Sorry about that.

00:17:10.170 --> 00:17:13.670
Please, that's in the past. Don't worry about it.

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:16.370
I've heard from the people in charge at the company

00:17:16.370 --> 00:17:20.640
that you're developing a robot like our cyber dolls.

00:17:21.220 --> 00:17:24.600
Well, I'm not nearly that good, but...

00:17:24.600 --> 00:17:30.380
You're far too modest. Was that cyber doll of use to you at all?

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:32.110
Yes! Of course she was!

00:17:32.590 --> 00:17:37.030
We have a great deal of interest in people like you, who dedicate their lives to study.

00:17:37.740 --> 00:17:42.480
If you like, I can give you a cyber doll to use in your research.

00:17:42.480 --> 00:17:43.790
What do you say?

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.230
S-Sure!

00:17:45.230 --> 00:17:46.330
Very well!

00:18:05.480 --> 00:18:06.890
H-He's so fast!

00:18:13.710 --> 00:18:14.820
What?

00:18:16.160 --> 00:18:19.430
Cyber dolls are made in countless variations.

00:18:19.430 --> 00:18:21.430
Please choose one that you like.

00:18:21.430 --> 00:18:26.200
Um... What happens to cyber dolls you repossess?

00:18:26.630 --> 00:18:32.140
They're taken to the maintenance factory for a service check and then stored until a new order is received.

00:18:32.140 --> 00:18:33.590
Why do you ask?

00:18:33.590 --> 00:18:34.980
Wh-What about their memories?!

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:37.360
They're kept intact.

00:18:37.360 --> 00:18:40.050
We reset them when the new order comes in.

00:18:40.590 --> 00:18:44.010
By the way, have you decided on which type yet?

00:18:44.920 --> 00:18:46.270
Um, well...

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.320
Yes?

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:49.250
Yeah...

00:18:50.440 --> 00:18:54.190
Then, I'd like May, please.

00:18:54.190 --> 00:18:58.990
That's a standard-grade model. There are much better ones.

00:18:59.370 --> 00:19:01.450
No, I want May back.

00:19:01.450 --> 00:19:03.700
I want the May that I had before!

00:19:05.820 --> 00:19:07.150
As you wish.

00:19:12.470 --> 00:19:13.750
Wait a second.

00:19:13.750 --> 00:19:15.050
Shall I cancel this?

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.920
N-No.

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:18.750
It's just...

00:19:18.750 --> 00:19:22.720
Could I be the one to make the final "okay" click, please?

00:19:24.630 --> 00:19:25.680
I understand.

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:26.910
Go ahead.

00:19:34.690 --> 00:19:36.650
What's wrong?

00:19:36.990 --> 00:19:41.360
Look... I don't have the money to pay for this.

00:19:42.300 --> 00:19:43.950
Then how about this?

00:19:44.370 --> 00:19:48.500
We'll say this is in return for the milk you gave me before.

00:19:48.500 --> 00:19:49.620
Yes, sir!

00:20:08.310 --> 00:20:12.370
Things just don't work out that easily, do they?

00:20:46.140 --> 00:20:47.890
You dropped the ribbon.

00:21:06.990 --> 00:21:09.410
Will you tie it on for me again?

00:21:16.220 --> 00:21:18.050
I'm back, Kazuya.

00:21:21.040 --> 00:21:22.680
Welcome home, May.

00:21:37.740 --> 00:21:46.650
When I'm with you, I blush till my ears turn red.

00:21:46.650 --> 00:21:51.010
I wonder why that is...

00:21:51.010 --> 00:21:57.080
When I'm alone with you I can never seem to do anything right.

00:21:57.080 --> 00:22:05.050
I become so tongue-tied I can't speak at all.

00:22:05.050 --> 00:22:12.230
It's strange, don't you think? I think about it too much.

00:22:12.230 --> 00:22:21.640
Is this love? I just can't accept that at all.

00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:28.380
I can't be honest. I want so much to be.

00:22:28.380 --> 00:22:35.060
Someday, perhaps, you'll tell me

00:22:35.060 --> 00:22:43.080
the true feelings that are in my heart.

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:46.270
Yo, Kei?

00:22:46.270 --> 00:22:47.510
Yo?

00:22:47.510 --> 00:22:49.470
I hear you don't get along with the telephone, Kei.

00:22:49.470 --> 00:22:50.170
How so?

00:22:50.170 --> 00:22:53.270
Kei Tai Denwa! Get it?

00:22:53.270 --> 00:22:54.470
Bad joke, huh?

00:22:54.470 --> 00:22:56.630
It's worse than one of Nanbara's jokes.

00:22:57.580 --> 00:22:59.890
"More! More!"
